/// Real plans as published, at the grain of their source (see Plan Grain): OSCAR Plans by organisation to 2021-22, Estimates by Spending Review group from 2022-23, PESA departmental AME and administration budgets by group to 2028-29. Held for the year, not by month; compare with outturn only at the plan's grain or coarser. GBP thousands. Source view dw.v_model_fact_plan.
table 'Fact Plan'
	lineageTag: fbab6938-a069-50fa-9e7e-c9a3a1c6b615

	/// Published plan in GBP thousands, summed over the plan rows in context, BLANK wherever the filter context is finer than the grain the plan is published at (a month, a sub-segment, an economic category, a department, a data quality issue, and an organisation, control budget or economic budget where the source has none). Grain A (OSCAR Plans) is published by organisation, control budget detail and economic budget, so a selection of those on the outturn side narrows the plan to the same codes. Administration budgets are part of resource DEL and are left out unless a Plan measure is chosen. Plan measures overlap by design; choose one to read it on its own.
	measure Plan =
			IF (
			    Grain.BelowGrain ( FALSE () ),
			    BLANK (),
			    CALCULATE (
			        SUM ( 'Fact Plan'[Plan Amount] ),
			        Plan.RowsInScope ( ISFILTERED ( 'Fact Plan'[Plan Measure] ) )
			    )
			)
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Plan
		lineageTag: 248e8154-1620-5d1c-9f1d-f1c2470ef7e6

	/// 1 where Plan is BLANK because the filter context is finer than the grain the plan is published at, otherwise 0. Use it to say "plan not published at this level" next to a blank.
	measure 'Plan Below Grain' = IF ( Grain.BelowGrain ( FALSE () ), 1, 0 )
		formatString: 0
		displayFolder: Plan
		lineageTag: 12c55800-7b7f-5642-a9c7-98e38052efc7

	/// The published plan of the statement line in context, in GBP thousands, only on a line that sits at a plan's grain: the net resource line (economic budget RESOURCE), the net capital line (CAPITAL) and the total line (every account), and only in a year where the source publishes a plan at that level (the OSCAR Plans years for RESOURCE and CAPITAL; every year with a plan for the total). The voted budgets only: RDEL, RDEL_EX_DEPN, CDEL, RAME, CAME. BLANK on every other line.
	measure 'Statement Plan' = Pnl.AtPlanScope ( [Plan] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Statement
		lineageTag: d7b11670-3415-4340-a5c0-65e60d5d06aa

	/// [Plan] in 2025-26 prices, in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative as in the nominal measure. Each financial year in context is multiplied by the GDP deflator index of 2025-26 divided by the index of that year (HM Treasury, default vintage October 2026 Budget, chained index: forecast years are chained from that one vintage), and the years are added. A month takes the index of its financial year. BLANK when a year that has an amount has no index, never the nominal figure. Under Time Intelligence, PY is the previous year in 2025-26 prices, YoY is the real change and YoY % the real growth rate. The Deflator table is related to nothing; the index is matched to the year with TREATAS inside Real.Deflate.
	measure 'Plan (real terms)' = Real.Deflate ( [Plan] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Real Terms
		lineageTag: 511cc7f2-aada-4b90-ab0a-ddc4c38f90c6

	/// The plan badge: the plan source and edition, and the grain it is published at, of the plan rows in the filter context (the year in view), for example a Supplementary Estimate at financial year x department group x measure. Several sources are joined with a semicolon. When the selection is finer than the plan's grain the text says the plan is blank, in the words the Plan measure follows. It is a label and holds no amount.
	measure 'Plan Source and Grain' =
			VAR Sources =
			    CALCULATETABLE (
			        SUMMARIZE ( 'Fact Plan', 'Plan Source'[Plan Source], 'Plan Grain'[Plan Grain] ),
			        Plan.RowsInScope ( ISFILTERED ( 'Fact Plan'[Plan Measure] ) )
			    )
			VAR Names =
			    CONCATENATEX ( Sources, 'Plan Source'[Plan Source] & " at " & 'Plan Grain'[Plan Grain], "; ", 'Plan Source'[Plan Source], ASC )
			RETURN
			    IF (
			        COUNTROWS ( Sources ) = 0,
			        "No plan is published for this selection",
			        Names & IF ( Grain.BelowGrain ( FALSE () ), ". The selection is finer than the plan's grain, so the plan is blank.", "" )
			    )
		displayFolder: Plan
		lineageTag: 1a3ab78d-79bd-5a08-9a33-e185c74c6310

		annotation BestPracticeAnalyzer_IgnoreRules = {"RuleIDs":["UKFR_MEASURE_FOLDER_AND_FORMAT","UKFR_MEASURE_FORMAT_IN_SET"]}

	/// Plan on the Plan scenario and outturn on the plan's basis on the Outturn scenario (read with the Scenario filter removed, because the plan rows that define the basis sit on the Plan scenario), in one measure, so that a waterfall can take Scenario as its category and a department group as its breakdown. BLANK for every other scenario and when more than one scenario is in context. Plan keeps its grain guard, so it is BLANK where it is not published.
	measure 'Plan and Outturn by Scenario' =
			SWITCH (
			    SELECTEDVALUE ( Scenario[Scenario] ),
			    "Plan", [Plan],
			    "Outturn", CALCULATE ( [Outturn (plan basis)], REMOVEFILTERS ( Scenario ) ),
			    BLANK ()
			)
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Plan
		lineageTag: 05570420-11de-50a0-970d-a9a6a7634367

	/// [Statement Plan] in 2025-26 prices, in GBP thousands, spending positive and income negative as in the nominal measure. Each financial year in context is multiplied by the GDP deflator index of 2025-26 divided by the index of that year (HM Treasury, default vintage October 2026 Budget, chained index: forecast years are chained from that one vintage), and the years are added. A month takes the index of its financial year. BLANK when a year that has an amount has no index, never the nominal figure. Under Time Intelligence, PY is the previous year in 2025-26 prices, YoY is the real change and YoY % the real growth rate. The Deflator table is related to nothing; the index is matched to the year with TREATAS inside Real.Deflate.
	measure 'Statement Plan (real terms)' = Real.Deflate ( [Statement Plan] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Real Terms
		lineageTag: a47a2461-3080-4079-b84d-9db8a786610b

